-- allium: 3
-- external-executor.allium
--
-- Scope: The ownership boundary between Weft and an external scheduler /
--        control plane (currently SkyPilot only), and the minimal
--        observability Weft mirrors from it.
-- Includes:
--   - What each side owns, expressed as an adapter contract
--   - Adapter availability as a three-state condition (reachable /
--     unreachable / not configured) and what each state may conclude
--   - What an observation is, and the three non-observation causes that are
--     UNKNOWN rather than terminal
--   - The unbound-job state left behind when submit records the ledger row
--     but the external submission does not confirm
--   - Staleness of a mirrored status, and how it must surface
--   - The explicit non-guarantees, stated as invariants rather than prose
-- Excludes:
--   - The ExternalJobBinding entity, `weft sky submit`, and `weft sky import`
--     (see job-lifecycle.allium § ExternalJobBinding,
--      § SubmitExternalExecutorJob, § ImportExternalExecutorJob)
--   - When sync fires and what it writes on a good observation
--     (see status-sync.allium § SyncExternalExecutorJob), and cancel
--     passthrough (§ ExternalExecutorCancel)
--   - Grouped-status bucket definitions and selected-job detail layout
--     (see status-sync.allium § TUIPeriodicSync); this file constrains only
--     what those surfaces must and must not say about external jobs
--   - Log import, artifact import, cost import, and in-cluster telemetry.
--     These are "later deepening" in docs/planning/skypilot-backend.md and
--     are deliberately *not* specified; several are ruled out below.
--
-- Design source: docs/planning/skypilot-backend.md (the decision) and
-- docs/design/comparison-to-skypilot.md (why Weft is not built on SkyPilot).
-- The rejected alternative was "SkyPilot as a cloud.Client provider facade".
-- SkyPilot is a scheduler/control plane, not a low-level provider like
-- Vast.ai or RunPod, so a provider-shaped integration would put two
-- schedulers in charge of one cluster's lifecycle.

use "./job-lifecycle.allium" as jobs
use "./status-sync.allium" as status_sync
use "./job-move.allium" as move

-- ==========================================================================
-- External Entities
-- ==========================================================================

-- The external scheduler itself. Weft neither installs, configures, starts,
-- nor supervises it. Its presence on the machine is a user decision, and its
-- absence is a normal, supported configuration.
external entity ExternalExecutorProcess {
    executor: jobs/ExternalExecutor
}

-- ==========================================================================
-- Value Types
-- ==========================================================================

-- Whether the executor adapter can be consulted at all, right now, on this
-- machine. Three states, not two — a `nil` answer must always arrive with the
-- reason that produced it.
--
--   reachable       the adapter answered
--   unreachable     the adapter exists but did not answer (timeout, error,
--                   auth failure, transport failure)
--   not_configured  the adapter is not installed here at all
--
-- `not_configured` is a *confirmed absence of the lever*, never a confirmed
-- absence of a job. Both non-reachable states yield UNKNOWN job state.
value ExecutorReachability = reachable | unreachable | not_configured

-- Why an observation attempt produced no state. Every one of these is
-- UNKNOWN. None of them is evidence that a job ended.
--
--   executor_not_configured  the `sky` CLI (or equivalent) is not installed
--   query_failed             installed, but the query errored or timed out
--   identity_not_listed      the executor answered, and this identity was not
--                            in the answer. Executors prune finished work
--                            from their queues, so absence from a listing is
--                            an ageing-out, not an outcome
--   binding_missing          Weft has a job row but no external identity to
--                            ask about (see UnconfirmedExternalSubmission)
value UnknownCause = executor_not_configured | query_failed
                   | identity_not_listed | binding_missing

-- The idempotency key for a mirrored job. Import and submit are both
-- idempotent on this triple; re-observing the same identity refreshes the
-- existing binding rather than creating a second local job.
value ExternalIdentity {
    executor: jobs/ExternalExecutor
    external_job_id: String
    external_task_id: String?
}

-- One attempt to observe an external job. `available` is the single gate the
-- writer in status-sync.allium § SyncExternalExecutorJob branches on; when it
-- is false, `unknown_cause` says why and every other field is absent.
value ExternalObservation {
    available: Boolean
    unknown_cause: UnknownCause?    -- non-null iff available = false

    raw_status: String?
    message: String?
    exit_code: Integer?
    normalized_status: jobs/Status?
    external_cluster_id: String?
    external_cluster_name: String?
    dashboard_url: String?
    observed_at: Timestamp?         -- non-null iff available = true
    error: String?                  -- transport/adapter error text, if any
}

-- The conservative subset of Weft run intent that survives translation into
-- an external task definition. Anything not listed here is not carried: Weft
-- does not attempt to reproduce its own placement, staging, or artifact model
-- inside the external executor's task.
value ExternalSubmitRequest {
    command: String
    working_dir: String
    gpu_class: String?
    gpu_count: Integer?
    gpu_mem_gb: Integer?
    env_vars: List<String>
    description: String?
}

-- ==========================================================================
-- Contracts
-- ==========================================================================

-- The full ownership boundary. Everything below the signatures is a property
-- of the boundary, not of any one call.
contract ExternalExecutorAdapter {
    reachability: () -> ExecutorReachability
    observe: (identity: ExternalIdentity) -> ExternalObservation
    submit: (request: ExternalSubmitRequest) -> ExternalIdentity
    cancel: (identity: ExternalIdentity) -> Boolean
    logs: (identity: ExternalIdentity) -> String

    @invariant ExecutorOwnsExecution
        -- The external executor selects cloud resources, provisions and tears
        -- down clusters, recovers preempted spot capacity, applies its own
        -- retry policy, and runs the task. Weft does not second-guess any of
        -- these, does not race them, and does not repair them.

    @invariant WeftOwnsTheLedger
        -- Weft owns the durable local job identity, project association,
        -- tags, processed bookkeeping, and every agent- and human-facing
        -- query surface. These are Weft-local facts; the executor is never
        -- consulted for them and never authoritative over them.

    @invariant OptInIfInstalled
        -- The adapter is CLI-shaped and optional. When it is not installed,
        -- the integration is a lever that is not available on this machine —
        -- not a fault. Reachability is answered by a bounded local probe
        -- (binary lookup plus a cheap liveness call), the same shape as
        -- cloud.Client.Available(). A not_configured answer must never
        -- produce an error status on a job, a user-facing failure for a
        -- command that did not ask for the executor, or a mutation of any
        -- job, attempt, or binding row.

    @invariant SilenceIsNotTermination
        -- No absence of an answer is an outcome. An uninstalled adapter, a
        -- timed-out query, an unlisted identity, and a missing binding are
        -- all UNKNOWN. The adapter must return the cause alongside the empty
        -- result so its caller can distinguish "looked and it was not there"
        -- from "could not look". Only a positively observed terminal status
        -- from the executor may move a mirrored job to a terminal state.

    @invariant LedgerBeforeExternalSubmit
        -- submit is called only after the local job row exists and is
        -- durable. A crash between the two must leave a recoverable local
        -- record, never an external job with no ledger entry. The reverse
        -- ordering would produce work that is running and being billed with
        -- no wj id to address, cancel, or attribute it.

    @invariant IdempotentOnIdentity
        -- observe and submit are idempotent on ExternalIdentity. Re-observing
        -- a known identity refreshes its binding; it never creates a second
        -- local job for the same external work.

    @guidance
        -- Implementation anchor: internal/skypilot/skypilot.go
        --   Client.Runner defaults to CLIRunner, which shells out to `sky`.
        --   Runner is an interface so tests substitute fixture output; the
        --   fixture path is the only sanctioned way to exercise these rules
        --   without SkyPilot installed.
        -- Adapter surface today: `sky jobs queue --output json` (observe),
        -- `sky jobs launch` (submit), `sky jobs cancel` (cancel),
        -- `sky jobs logs` (logs).
}

-- ==========================================================================
-- Config
-- ==========================================================================

config {
    -- Bounded probe for "is this lever available here". Kept small: it runs
    -- on paths that did not ask for the executor.
    reachability_probe_timeout: Duration = 2.seconds

    -- Budget for one observation pass. Shared with the sync side so a slow
    -- executor cannot spend a TUI refresh budget that belongs to SSH and
    -- cloud-provider work.
    observe_timeout: Duration = status_sync/config.external_sync_timeout

    -- A mirrored status is only as good as its last successful observation.
    -- Past this age, surfaces must say so rather than presenting the cached
    -- status as current.
    observation_stale_after: Duration = 10.minutes

    -- How long a Weft job row may exist with backend = skypilot and no
    -- binding before surfaces call the submission unconfirmed.
    unconfirmed_submission_after: Duration = 5.minutes
}

-- ==========================================================================
-- Rules
-- ==========================================================================

-- Entry point for the refresh pass that status-sync.allium § ExplicitSync and
-- § TUIPeriodicSync emit but do not themselves consume. One reachability
-- probe per pass, not per job.
rule ExternalExecutorRefreshPass {
    when: ExternalExecutorSyncTriggered(external_jobs)

    let reachability = ExecutorReachability(config.reachability_probe_timeout)

    -- The lever is not available on this machine. Report it once, at pass
    -- level, and touch nothing. This is not a per-job condition and must not
    -- be rendered as one.
    if reachability = not_configured:
        ensures: ExternalExecutorLeverAbsent(skypilot)

    else:
        -- An unbound job has no identity to ask about. It is not an error
        -- here; UnconfirmedExternalSubmission surfaces it on its own clock.
        for job in external_jobs
            where exists(jobs/ExternalJobBinding { job = job }):
                let binding = jobs/ExternalJobBinding { job = job }
                ensures: ExternalObservationRequested(binding, config.observe_timeout)
                ensures: status_sync/SyncJobTriggered(job, status_only)

    @guidance
        -- The probe is what keeps `weft sync`, `weft jobs list`, and the TUI
        -- tick cheap and quiet on machines with no SkyPilot install: they
        -- must not emit per-job warnings, must not print an error, and must
        -- not spend the observe budget discovering the same absence once per
        -- mirrored job.
        --
        -- Commands that explicitly named the executor (`weft sky sync`,
        -- `weft sky import`, `weft sky submit`) MAY surface not_configured as
        -- a command-level error, because the user asked for the lever by
        -- name. Ambient refresh paths MUST NOT.
}

-- Defines the observation that status-sync.allium § SyncExternalExecutorJob
-- branches on. This rule owns what may be concluded; that rule owns what is
-- then written.
rule ClassifyExternalObservation {
    when: ExternalObservationRequested(binding, timeout)

    let reachability = ExecutorReachability(config.reachability_probe_timeout)

    if reachability = not_configured:
        ensures: ExternalObservation(
            available: false,
            unknown_cause: executor_not_configured
        )
        ensures: ExternalObservationUnavailable(binding, executor_not_configured)

    else if reachability = unreachable:
        ensures: ExternalObservation(
            available: false,
            unknown_cause: query_failed,
            error: ExecutorProbeError()
        )
        ensures: ExternalObservationUnavailable(binding, query_failed)

    else:
        let row = ExternalExecutorRow(binding, timeout)

        -- The executor answered and did not mention this identity. Executors
        -- age finished work out of their queues on their own schedule, so
        -- this says nothing about how the job ended, or whether it has.
        if row = null:
            ensures: ExternalObservation(
                available: false,
                unknown_cause: identity_not_listed
            )
            ensures: ExternalObservationUnavailable(binding, identity_not_listed)

        else:
            ensures: ExternalObservation(
                available: true,
                raw_status: row.status,
                message: row.message,
                exit_code: row.exit_code,
                normalized_status: NormalizeExternalStatus(row.status),
                external_cluster_id: row.cluster_id,
                external_cluster_name: row.cluster_name,
                dashboard_url: row.dashboard_url,
                observed_at: now
            )

    @guidance
        -- This rule defines the value that status-sync.allium
        -- § SyncExternalExecutorJob binds as
        --   QueryExternalExecutor(executor, external_job_id, external_task_id,
        --                         timeout)
        -- and branches on via `observation.available`. The identity triple
        -- and timeout are carried on the binding and the request; the split
        -- keeps "what may be concluded" here and "what is then written" there.
        --
        -- Normalization is coarse and bucket-oriented; the mapping table and
        -- the unknown-state fallbacks live with the writer in
        -- status-sync.allium § SyncExternalExecutorJob.
        --
        -- The `row = null` branch is the one most likely to be "helpfully"
        -- simplified later. Do not fold it into a terminal status. Weft's
        -- recurring bug class is treating a failed or empty lookup as a
        -- confirmed negative; the mirrored-status case is the same shape as
        -- the nil-provider-instance and stale-heartbeat incidents.
}

-- A refresh that produced no observation records the cause and advances
-- nothing. Kept separate from the writer so the "leave it alone" obligations
-- are stated once, positively.
rule ExternalObservationLeavesStateAlone {
    when: ExternalObservationUnavailable(binding, cause)

    ensures: binding.job.status unchanged
    ensures: binding.raw_status unchanged
    ensures: binding.raw_status_message unchanged
    ensures: binding.normalized_status unchanged
    ensures: binding.last_observed_at unchanged
    ensures: ExternalSyncWarningRecorded(binding, cause)

    @guidance
        -- last_observed_at is the timestamp of the last *successful*
        -- observation, and is the input to the staleness surface. Stamping it
        -- on a failed refresh would make an unobserved job look freshly
        -- confirmed, which is precisely the reading the staleness warning
        -- exists to prevent.
        --
        -- The staleness warning is a Weft-side fact about Weft's own
        -- observation, and the executor's last reported message is an
        -- executor-side fact. They are separate observable values; recording
        -- one must not overwrite the other.
}

-- `weft sky submit` writes the ledger row first (job-lifecycle.allium
-- § SubmitExternalExecutorJob). This rule specifies the window between the
-- two writes: a Weft job with an external backend and no external identity.
--
-- Reached by three paths:
--   (a) the process died between the row write and the binding write;
--   (b) the external submit was attempted and definitively refused — that
--       path is terminal and is owned by SubmitExternalExecutorJob, which
--       closes the attempt as dead with the submission error;
--   (c) the external submit was attempted and its outcome is unknown (the
--       call timed out, or it succeeded but the external id could not be
--       resolved afterwards).
--
-- Only (b) is terminal. (a) and (c) are UNKNOWN: the external work may well
-- be running and billing. Weft must not guess.
rule UnconfirmedExternalSubmission {
    when: job: jobs/Job.created_at + config.unconfirmed_submission_after <= now
    requires: job.backend = skypilot
    requires: not job.is_terminal
    requires: not exists(jobs/ExternalJobBinding { job = job })

    ensures: job.status unchanged
    ensures: ExternalSubmissionUnconfirmed(job, binding_missing)

    @guidance
        -- The job is recoverable-by-construction: it has a wj id, a project,
        -- a command, and a working directory, so a user or agent can rebind
        -- it with `weft sky import` once the external id is known, or cancel
        -- it locally.
        --
        -- What it must NOT do while unconfirmed:
        --   - become failed/dead on its own. Nothing has been observed.
        --   - be picked up by Weft placement, autopilot, or move. The job's
        --     target kind is external_executor, so it is not unplaced work.
        --     See ExternalJobsExcludedFromWeftPlacement.
        --   - be synced. status-sync.allium § SyncExternalExecutorJob is
        --     guarded on the binding existing, so an unbound job is simply
        --     not observable, which is exactly the binding_missing cause.
        --
        -- Divergence to resolve: `weft sky submit --dry-run-task` currently
        -- creates a durable job row and then returns without submitting, so
        -- every dry run leaves a permanently unconfirmed job. See the open
        -- question on dry-run rows.
}

-- Surfacing rule: which grouped-status bucket a mirrored job lands in.
rule BucketExternalExecutorJob {
    when: JobBucketAssigned(job)
    requires: job.backend = skypilot

    ensures: JobBucketedAs(job, BucketForStatus(job.status))

    @guidance
        -- The bucket is driven only by the normalized Job.status already
        -- stored in the DB. Raw executor statuses are detail, never bucket
        -- input. Bucket definitions live in status-sync.allium
        -- § TUIPeriodicSync.
        --
        -- The bug this rule exists to prevent: bucketing derived from the
        -- presence of a Host or Launch row files every external job under
        -- Unplaced, where it reads as work Weft has failed to place and
        -- invites the autopilot-stuck-queue reading. An external job has no
        -- Host and no Launch by design — target_kind = external_executor
        -- means another scheduler owns placement, and that is a completed
        -- state of affairs, not a pending one.
}

-- Surfacing rule: what the target line and detail block may say.
rule RenderExternalExecutorTarget {
    when: JobTargetLineRendered(job)
    requires: job.backend = skypilot

    let binding = jobs/ExternalJobBinding { job = job }

    if not exists binding:
        ensures: TargetLineRendered(job, external_binding_unavailable)

    else:
        let observation_age = now - binding.last_observed_at

        ensures: TargetLineRendered(job, ExternalTargetDescription(binding))

        if binding.last_observed_at = null
           or observation_age > config.observation_stale_after:
            ensures: StaleObservationWarningRendered(job, observation_age)

    @guidance
        -- Content available, and nothing beyond it: executor name, external
        -- job id, external task id, cluster name/id, raw status, raw status
        -- message, dashboard URL, and the last-observed timestamp. These are
        -- what the executor's task-info output already yields; each is free.
        --
        -- The line must not imply a Weft-managed instance, a Weft cost meter,
        -- a grace period, an R2 phase, or agent telemetry. None of those
        -- exist for this job, and rendering a placeholder for them (a dash, a
        -- zero cost, an empty phase) reads as "Weft measured this and got
        -- nothing" rather than "Weft does not measure this". Omit the
        -- segment.
        --
        -- The staleness warning is not optional decoration. A mirrored status
        -- is a cached observation; without an age next to it, a job that
        -- finished an hour ago and a job Weft has not been able to reach for
        -- an hour are indistinguishable on screen.
        --
        -- Implementation anchors: cmd/list.go printExternalBindingSummary,
        -- and the external-executor branch of the selected-job Host line in
        -- status-sync.allium § TUIPeriodicSync.
}

-- ==========================================================================
-- Invariants
-- ==========================================================================

-- The bounded shape, stated so that wiring one of these up is a spec change
-- and not a quiet enhancement. Each is a thing a future contributor could
-- reasonably believe is an oversight rather than a decision.

invariant ExternalJobsHaveNoWeftInstanceRows {
    -- No Launch, no CloudInstance, no inventory Host. Weft did not rent the
    -- machine this job runs on and has no lifecycle authority over it, so
    -- there is nothing for these rows to describe. Creating them would put
    -- Weft's instance reconciler, watchdogs, and teardown paths in charge of
    -- a cluster the external executor owns.
    for job in jobs/Jobs:
        job.backend = skypilot implies
            job.host = null
            and job.cloud_instance = null
            and job.latest_attempt.cloud_instance = null
}

invariant ExternalJobsCarryNoWeftCostMeter {
    -- Weft's cost figures come from its own rental meter: provider hourly
    -- rate multiplied by observed instance uptime. There is no such meter
    -- here. Importing the executor's own cost estimate is a candidate for
    -- later deepening, and would need to be visibly distinguished from a
    -- metered figure rather than merged into the same field.
    for job in jobs/Jobs:
        job.backend = skypilot implies job.cost = null
}

invariant ExternalJobsExcludedFromWeftPlacement {
    -- Placement scoring, the survival model, and move all act on jobs Weft
    -- can put somewhere. An external job's placement already happened,
    -- elsewhere. An open PlacementIntent or MoveIntent on one of these jobs
    -- means some path is treating it as Weft-schedulable work.
    for job in jobs/Jobs:
        job.backend = skypilot implies
            not exists(move/PlacementIntent { job = job, state = open })
            and not exists(move/MoveIntent { job = job, state = open })
}

invariant ExternalIdentityIsUnique {
    -- Duplicate-import protection. Two bindings sharing the idempotency key
    -- means two local jobs are mirroring one piece of external work, and any
    -- observation will write conflicting status to both.
    for a in jobs/ExternalJobBindings:
        for b in jobs/ExternalJobBindings:
            a != b implies
                not (a.executor = b.executor
                     and a.external_job_id = b.external_job_id
                     and a.external_task_id = b.external_task_id)
}

invariant ObservationTimestampImpliesObservation {
    -- last_observed_at is stamped by successful observation only. If it can
    -- be advanced without a raw status to show for it, the staleness surface
    -- is reporting Weft's own retry cadence rather than its contact with the
    -- executor, and a job nobody has been able to reach looks fresh.
    for binding in jobs/ExternalJobBindings:
        binding.last_observed_at != null implies binding.raw_status != null
}

invariant MirroredStatusAgreesWithBinding {
    -- The binding's normalized_status is advisory until the sync writer
    -- copies it to Job.status; once an observation has landed, the two agree.
    -- Nothing else derives a stored job status from raw executor text, and no
    -- surface re-derives one at render time. (An in-flight cancel shows
    -- through the attempt's pending_status overlay, which does not touch the
    -- stored status this invariant ranges over.)
    for binding in jobs/ExternalJobBindings:
        binding.last_observed_at != null
            implies binding.normalized_status = binding.job.status
}

-- ==========================================================================
-- Surfaces
-- ==========================================================================

surface ExternalExecutorIntegration {
    facing executor: ExternalExecutorProcess

    context binding: jobs/ExternalJobBinding

    exposes:
        binding.executor
        binding.external_job_id
        binding.external_task_id
        binding.external_cluster_id
        binding.external_cluster_name
        binding.raw_status
        binding.raw_status_message
        binding.dashboard_url
        binding.normalized_status
        binding.last_observed_at

    contracts:
        demands ExternalExecutorAdapter

    @guarantee WeftRunsNothingInsideTheCluster
        -- Weft deploys no agent, no wrapper, and no runner into an external
        -- executor's cluster, and injects no WEFT_* environment variables
        -- into the task. The task definition is the conservative translation
        -- in ExternalSubmitRequest and nothing more. Everything Weft knows
        -- about this job's execution comes from the executor's own task-info
        -- output.

    @guarantee NoWeftDurabilityOrTelemetryPromised
        -- No R2 output streaming, no artifact collection, no per-job
        -- telemetry time series, no grace period, no benchmark isolation, no
        -- disk estimation, no interruptible pause/resume modelling. These are
        -- properties of Weft's own agent on Weft's own rental substrate.
        -- Surfaces must not offer them for external jobs, and must not render
        -- empty placeholders that imply they were attempted.

    @guarantee ProcessedRemainsWeftLocal
        -- The processed/unprocessed distinction is a Weft tag on the local
        -- job row. Executor task state, cluster tags, and task labels are
        -- never read as the processed marker and never written to reflect it.
        -- See job-lifecycle.allium § ExternalJobsUseWeftBookkeeping.

    @guarantee LocalIdIsTheAddress
        -- wj<id> is the canonical address for both imported and
        -- Weft-submitted external jobs, in every command, message, and view.
        -- The external id is detail: shown where it helps a user reach the
        -- executor's own tooling, never required to address the job in Weft.
        -- See job-lifecycle.allium § ExternalJobIdentityIsLocal.

    @guarantee ObservationChannelIsSeparateFromExecutorMessage
        -- The executor's last reported status message and Weft's own
        -- staleness/failure warning are distinct observable values. A failed
        -- refresh may add the second; it may not overwrite the first. Losing
        -- the executor's last message to a transport error deletes the most
        -- recent thing actually known about the job.

    @guidance
        -- Implementation anchors:
        --   internal/skypilot/skypilot.go   — adapter (CLIRunner, Client)
        --   internal/db/external_jobs.go    — binding storage, idempotent
        --                                     upsert on the identity triple
        --   cmd/sky.go                      — submit / import / sync, and the
        --                                     log and cancel passthroughs
        --   cmd/list.go                     — printExternalBindingSummary
        --
        -- Adding a second executor means adding a value to
        -- jobs/ExternalExecutor and a second adapter behind this contract. It
        -- does not mean generalising Weft's provider layer: the boundary here
        -- is scheduler-to-scheduler, not scheduler-to-provider.
}

-- ==========================================================================
-- Open Questions
-- ==========================================================================

-- RESOLVED: exit_code stays null for external-executor jobs. SkyPilot's job
-- queue reports a status, not a process exit code — skypilot.Job carries no
-- such field and ParseJobsQueueJSON never populates one — so any value written
-- would be derived from the status and indistinguishable from an observation.
-- A reader seeing exit_code=1 would conclude the process exited 1, when it may
-- have been killed at 137 or never have run. Every reader was checked and is
-- nil-guarded; failure classification keys on status first and consults
-- exit_code only to refine the completed case, so a failed external job still
-- classifies as failed. Terminal outcome is carried by normalized status, the
-- executor's own account by raw_status / raw_status_message.
-- Implementation: internal/db/external_jobs.go insertExternalAttempt and
-- updateExternalAttemptTx.

-- RESOLVED for now: multiple bindings per job cannot arise today, so
-- highest-id-wins is defensive rather than load-bearing. AttachExternalBinding
-- has one call site and runs once per `weft sky submit`; import goes through
-- the upsert keyed on external identity; and `weft restart` has no
-- external-executor path at all. The question becomes live only if external
-- retry is implemented, and the answer should be chosen then rather than
-- inherited from the ORDER BY.
--
-- Note the adjacent gap this exposed: `weft restart` on a backend=skypilot job
-- is unhandled rather than refused. It should either refuse with a clear
-- message or route to the executor; falling through to the rental/on-prem path
-- is not a third option.

-- RESOLVED: dry run skips the ledger write entirely. The ledger-before-external
-- ordering exists so a crash mid-submit leaves a recoverable record; a render
-- that submits nothing has nothing to recover, and the row it left behind had
-- no binding, so SyncExternalExecutorJob (guarded on the binding) could never
-- advance it. The task name in the rendered YAML is a documented placeholder,
-- since no job id is allocated. Implementation: cmd/sky.go runSkySubmit returns
-- before db.Open().

-- RESOLVED by removing the threshold from the surface. The observation age is
-- reported alongside a recorded sync warning rather than gated on a cutoff, so
-- there is no value to calibrate and no threshold that can turn healthy
-- managed-job recovery into noise. A threshold would only be needed if
-- staleness ever drove an action; it must not, since an unrefreshed status is
-- UNKNOWN, never terminal.
